  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Native routing",
      "items": [
        "Brain.respond sends a request with airfield: true or carrier_id to its native service under radio_lock and returns before any LLM code (brain.py 164-181).",
        "The local LLM fallback (brain.py 195-231) only serves AWACS and the limited JTAC path. It never interprets, authorises or validates native ATC or carrier calls.",
        "If a call enrols the pilot in one native family, the brain releases the unit from the other family (brain.py 172-180; release_unit airfield.py 1306-1317, carrier.py 593-605)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Frequency and coalition collisions",
      "items": [
        "Every radio uses the canonical channel coalition:frequency_hz:modulation. Two radios conflict when their frequencies are less than FREQUENCY_GUARD_HZ = 200 Hz apart (carrier.py 79).",
        "Airfield: a radio within 200 Hz of a reserved channel is disabled, whatever its coalition. Reserved channels are AWACS/JTAC plus the enabled carrier radios (__main__.py 83-100, brain.py 64-73, airfield.py 652-673).",
        "Airfield: a different channel of the same coalition within 200 Hz is disabled. Airdromes publishing exactly the same channel share one registry radio, and the caller must name the airfield (airfield.py 675-681, 1482-1509).",
        "Carrier: any other live carrier within 200 Hz disables the radio, whatever its coalition or modulation (carrier.py 512-517).",
        "RadioGateways checks the 200 Hz rule again. Airfield ids must be canonical channels, and every clashing entry is removed (radio_gateways.py 155-174)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Gateway topology",
      "items": [
        "Airfield: one Gateway per canonical channel, scoped airfield: true. The field and session are resolved inside AirfieldService (radio_gateways.py 1-8, 212).",
        "Carrier: one Gateway per carrier id, scoped carrier_id (radio_gateways.py 212-215).",
        "A changed spec (epoch, id, coalition, Hz, modulation, name, password) closes the old radio. If one radio fails to start, the others keep running (radio_gateways.py 201-219)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Reply gating",
      "items": [
        "Before transmitting, the Gateway checks the reply's scope (_bound), then POSTs /validate-event. A native reply without validation is dropped (gateway.py 256-273).",
        "Bridge snapshots require X-DCS-Token. Retired mission epochs are refused across both native roles (__main__.py 141-158, brain.py 75-91)."
      ]
    }
  ]
